From e0748b9fbadb610fa1f7a6ca7b9d32b992f3b0da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 23:03:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] game: bound guild emblem decoding and sandbox companion
 AI

A guild emblem arrives over the network as a zlib stream, and the decoder
accepted whatever dimensions it declared, so a 4 KiB payload could drive a
large allocation. Dimensions are now checked before decoding. Companion AI
scripts come from the data directory or a GRF, so they no longer reach
os.execute, io.popen, package.loadlib or the debug library, and io.open cannot
escape the data directory.
